+- No external dependencies beyond todomvc-common and todomvc-app-css
+
+## Leg 2 — Browser acceptance failures (product defects)
+
+### Defect 1: render() destroys and recreates all <li> nodes
+
+Root cause of 7/7 acceptance failures. The render() function at js/app.js:82-127
+iterates `while (todoList.firstChild) { todoList.removeChild(todoList.firstChild); }`
+then re-creates every `<li>` via `document.createElement('li')`. This destroys all
+DOM element identity before the browser's event lifecycle completes. Cypress holds a
+reference taken before the event, then finds the node detached.
+
+Cypress errors produced:
+- `cy.eq() failed because the page updated...subject is no longer attached to the DOM`
+  (toggle-all tests 1-2)
+- `cy.find() failed because the page updated...subject is no longer attached to the DOM`
+  (toggle tests 3-4)
+- `Failed to execute 'removeChild' on 'Node': The node to be removed is no longer a child`
+  (edit tests 5-7)
+
+### Fix required
+
+Render() must mutate existing <li> nodes in place:
+- Toggle completed: add/remove class `completed` on existing <li>, toggle checkbox
+- Toggle-all: same on all <li> elements, or add/remove the class
+- Add new items: append new <li> to the end (don't rebuild all)
+- Remove items: remove just that <li> from its parent (don't rebuild all)
+- Clear completed: remove only the completed <li> elements
+- Visibility filtering: show/hide existing <li> elements rather than re-rendering
+- Reordering: if sorting is needed (not in TodoMVC), move existing nodes
+
+### Current status
+
+- `features/todomvc-conformance.feature` — strengthened with new scenario that catches
+  the removeChild loop (RED on current code)
+- `watchbill.json` — created with watch-1 targeting the conformance scenario
+- Conformance rule `no-removechild-todolist` added to `.shipshape/conformance-rules.mjs`
+- Step definitions updated in `features/support/steps.js` to wire new conformance check
\ No newline at end of file
